From: lean <chenlin@fnnas.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: allow NanoPi R4S SD power cycling

The TF supply is switched through GPIO0_A1, but its inherited always-on
constraint prevents MMC initialization retries from switching it off.
Allow power cycling with a 200 ms off interval and a 5 ms startup delay.
NanoPi R4SE inherits the same supply. Keep the existing UHS restriction.

Signed-off-by: lean <chenlin@fnnas.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-nanopi-r4s.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-nanopi-r4s.dtsi
@@ -133,3 +133,10 @@
 &vcc3v3_sys {
 	vin-supply = <&vcc5v0_sys>;
 };
+
+&vcc3v0_sd {
+	/* Let MMC retries reset cards left busy during initialization. */
+	/delete-property/ regulator-always-on;
+	off-on-delay-us = <200000>;
+	startup-delay-us = <5000>;
+};
